			"date": "2023-10-03T18:13:13.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://hachyderm.io/@andydavies\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>andydavies</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Beautiful read, thanks for sharing. I am also in the process of rethinking our microfrontends based system and these experiences are golden. The only thing that left me a bit puzzled was the \"no shared frameworks/libraries/css in the browser\". I know it's hard to impl, but since they use a design system I believe that at least the CSS foundation should/could be shared</p>",
